<!-- @after 12. Further Reading :: recap -->
### Say these in the interview

- The backend owns trip transitions; a client action is a command, not proof that the trip advanced.
- Keep commandId stable across retries and recover the active trip from the server after process death.
- An online driver keeps user-visible location tracking running; periodic work is too stale for dispatch.
- Buffer pings by owner, upload with that owner’s credentials and delete acknowledged samples.
- Handle service loss explicitly: mark the driver stale server-side and offer a tap to resume tracking.
